# Capped below 2.0. MCP SDK 2.0.0 renames FastMCP -> MCPServer and moves the
# whole mcp.server.fastmcp.* namespace to mcp.server.mcpserver.*, so two of the
# symbols this server imports move on a 2.x jump: FastMCP (server.py, tools/*,
# resources/*) and ToolError (mcp.server.fastmcp.exceptions). The other two mcp
# imports -- mcp.types.ToolAnnotations and
# mcp.server.transport_security.TransportSecuritySettings -- are not named in
# the upstream migration guide, and that silence is not a stability guarantee:
# check them against an installed 2.x before the cap lifts. The migration is
# small (a rename plus import paths; the decorator API is unchanged upstream)
# but it is a code change, not a currency bump, and is tracked as its own bead
# (enhancedchannelmanager-wiezs). Lift the cap there, not in a dependency
# sweep -- an unpinned jump fails at import time.
# 1.30.0 bounds stateful Streamable HTTP sessions (CVE-2026-59951).
mcp[cli]>=1.30.0,<2
httpx>=0.28.0
# Remove compromised emSign ECC Root CA - G3; retain unaffected trust anchors.
# GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 (2026.10.18 removed additional unaffected roots).
certifi>=2026.10.19
uvicorn[standard]>=0.32.0
